## 7. Access-Control Results

The Effective Access evaluations demonstrate different access outcomes for the two test identities.

| User | Business Role | Security Group | Evaluated Finance Access |
|---|---|---|---|
| Alice Johnson | Finance Analyst | `DomConsultancy-Finance` | Read, write and execute when Finance group membership is included |
| Sarah Williams | IT Support Analyst | `DomConsultancy-IT-Support` | No effective access |

This configuration demonstrates group-based access control: permissions are assigned according to business responsibilities rather than directly to individual users.

It also highlights the importance of reviewing inherited permissions. Broad permissions inherited from a parent directory can unintentionally grant access to resources.

### Validation Limitation

Effective Access calculates permissions; it does not perform an actual sign-in or resource-access attempt.

Alice could not complete an interactive logon to the domain controller because of its logon restrictions. A separate Windows client or member workstation will be used later for a real end-user access test.

